A bounded-coordinate trial exposed a GSAS-II parameter-limit subtlety: coordinate-shift variables are checked against absolute coordinates, so naïve ±shift limits forced atoms toward the origin. I caught this in the saved rollback points; none of those trial files will be used. I’m restarting from the untouched accepted checkpoint with absolute coordinate windows and independent snapshots.

