A second profile basin was found without adding extra phases or texture: a physically ordinary isotropic-strain model reaches Rwp 3.42%, close to the 3.14% counting-statistical minimum. The earlier apparent extreme [110] anisotropy was only a route into this basin; once restarted there, both phases refine isotropically and the fit is stable. I’m checking whether any bounded anisotropy is genuinely supported before freezing the final model.

